      "side": 1,
      "message": "So `atest VtsHalIdentityTargetTest` will run against the IC HAL on the device in question ...\n\nIf you are using a device with the non-default IC HAL it will call into whatever IC HAL the OEM included there include the TA backing that HAL. And since this code - libeic - is used only in the TA it\u0027s anybody\u0027s question if it gets used. Most likely not since it\u0027s not clear the TA is using libeic at all or if it is, it might be using its own locally modified copy.\n\nIf you are using a device using the default IC HAL then you should be able to see changes right away.\n\nFor development I\u0027m usually using aosp_cf_x86_64_phone-userdebug (along with running the emulator binary) and this device uses the default IC HAL and in this setup development is really easy/snappy.\n\nWhat device were you using and what was the very unhappy response?",
      "parentUuid": "6d97458f_6ff7005a",
